00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
what happens when you paste the name of  a classic movie on a bad movie and call  the thing a sequel let's say the results  are less than stellar in the case of s  darko stick around to see the full list  of lame cinematic follow-ups  horror films and psychological thrillers  are gold mines for unnecessary add-ons  and plenty of franchises like hellraiser  and child's play for instance which have  spawned numerous sequels that don't add  much to the original story in many cases  these sequels end up going direct to  video or straight to streaming nowadays  which usually indicates that their  quality is substantially lower than the  original one of the most egregious  examples of this is the direct to video  sequel to mary herron's american psycho  the classic slasher film starring  christian bell as serial killer patrick  bateman released two years after the  original american psycho 2 all-american  girl stars mila kunis as a college  student who becomes a murderer during  her time studying criminology christian  bale isn't in the film but patrick  bateman does appear albeit played by  someone else with his face never shown  the connection to the first film is  small but that's because there was  originally no connection at all american  psycho 2 began as an original screenplay  called the girl who wouldn't die but was  undeservingly given the american psycho  title late in production in a  transparent bid to capitalize on the  original film's success it was a cheap  cash grab that definitely resulted in  more than a few disgruntled blockbuster  customers i have to return some  videotapes the blair witch project  changed the horror game when it arrived  in the summer of 1999. one of the  earliest examples of the modern found  footage genre the story of three film  students lost in the woods was an  unprecedented success that spawned a  sequel only a year later however it  wasn't originally supposed to be  released at least not that quickly after  the blair witch project broke the record  for the best budget to box office ratio  in american history its distributor  artisan entertainment wasted no time in  green lighting a second installment  while production company hacks and films  didn't want to rush it artisan pushed on  regardless choosing to move forward  without the involvement of either of the  original blair witch directors troop  crime documentarian joe burlinger took  the helm but even he was dissatisfied  with the final product after studio  executives made sweeping changes to his  initial vision the final product was  book of shadows blair witch 2 which came  and went with little fanfare or praise  the blair witch franchise was rebooted  with another installment in 2016 but the  magic of the first film still has yet to  be replicated and it's hard to believe  that it ever will be  the bourne identity kicked off the born  franchise with a bang telling the  exciting yet thoughtful story of an  amnesiac cia operative on a mission to  discover his past while not every film  in the series was universally acclaimed  the first three were positively received  bringing in a combined 950 million  dollars at the box office while the  bourne identity was an adaptation of the  first installment of robert ludlum's  best-selling trilogy of novels that  didn't mean that production on follow-up  film the bourne supremacy was a foregone  conclusion matt damon the face of four  out of five of the films in the  franchise has commented that the born  identity was never made with a trilogy  or even a sequel in mind according to  damon expectations were low due to a  number of production problems along with  the film's release date being the same  as the live-action scooby-doo even  though the mystery gang brought in a bit  more cash the bourne identity defied  expectations and revolutionized the  action genre for years to follow harold  remus caddyshack the 1980 comedy about  the workers and members of an elite golf  club features an all-star cast that  includes bill murray and chevy chase  after the pitcher surpassed expectations  and catapulted rodney dangerfield to big  screen stardom warner brothers requested  a sequel and things got complicated from  there production on caddyshack 2 was a  mess right from the start an initially  apathetic reimus only agreed to the  sequel at dangerfield's request but when  numerous story ideas and rewrites left  dangerfield unsatisfied he and remus  dropped out of the project a few months  later chevy chase was the only original  cast member who would end up appearing  in the sequel albeit in a smaller role  the actors who replaced the original  cast as well as their new characters  were the final nails in the coffin for  this troubled sequel with terrible  reviews and dismal box office returns  caddyshack 2 is a follow-up that  reaffirms that some ideas should just be  one and done  brian de palma's 1976 adaptation of  stephen king's carry is nothing less  than a horror classic the tale of a high  school outcast who wreaks telekinetic  havoc on her bullies has not only been  remade for film and television multiple  times over the years but also inspired a  sequel that was released a whole 23  years after the original set within the  same universe as the original film the  rage carrie 2 centers around a young  woman named rachel who has power similar  to carrie and uses them to exact revenge  on classmates who drove her only friend  to suicide much like american psycho 2  the rage carrie 2 started as an original  story but the powers that be thought  that making rachel and carrie related  would boost ticket sales despite the  return of amy irving as sue snell it  didn't work the rage carry 2 was panned  by critics and failed to make a profit  once a studio decides that it wants a  sequel there isn't much that can stop it  from happening but it definitely doesn't  help if the people responsible for the  original film want nothing to do with it  one filmmaker who was particularly  uninterested in returning under studio  control was richard kelly the filmmaker  behind the 2001 science fiction coming  of age film donnie darko although donnie  darko didn't do well financially on  initial release it's since gained a cult  following thanks to its enigmatic plot  that follows a troubled high schooler  who's seeing visions of a strange man in  a rabbit suit i met a new friend  real or imaginary  imaginary in 2009 the sequel s darko was  released centering around donnie's  youngest sister and featuring a  similarly strange plot according to  kelly however not only did he have no  involvement in esdarco but he's never  even seen the film and has no plans to  watch it anytime soon that's probably  for the best considering that critics  and moviegoers didn't seem to like it  either even though he hasn't released a  movie since the box in 2009 kelly has  promised his own d'arco follow-up in the  future  william friedkin's 1973 blockbuster the  exorcist is widely regarded as one of  the best horror films ever made  frightening in a way that few movies at  the time were able to match the battle  between two priests and the demon  possessing 12 year old reagan spawned a  franchise that includes several sequels  a television series and a reboot trilogy  slated for 2023 william peter blatty the  author of the novel the film is based on  produced the first film and wrote the  script winning the academy award for  best adapted screenplay since the  exorcist was one of the biggest films of  the 1970s warner brothers was hungry for  a sequel but neither blatty nor friedkin  were interested in signing on regardless  production on exorcist 2 the heretic  eventually went ahead with a new writer  new producers a new director and the  return of linda blair's reagan as a  young teenager dealing with the trauma  of the previous film's events whereas  the first film elicited scares the  sequel drew anger and laughter from both  critics and moviegoers failing to meet  financial expectations in the process  vlady eventually returned to write and  direct the exorcist 3 which was released  17 years after the original and  completely ignored the events of the  heretic the three cool got much better  reviews and has many more fans but it's  still not as universally beloved as the  original  sequels typically arrive no more than a  few years after the films they're  following up the odds of success tend to  fall the longer it takes but a long wait  can still end up with a big hit that  wasn't the case unfortunately for  gremlins 2 the new badge the sequel to  1984's gremlins showed up in theater six  years after the original and despite  earning positive reviews it had a dismal  box office run director joe dante didn't  want to make a gremlin sequel when  warner brothers originally asked but he  eventually agreed on the condition that  he could have full creative control  dante's vision resulted in a film that  saw gremlins invade a new york city  skyscraper featuring several instances  of wildly anarchic meta-humor the new  batch didn't catch on during its initial  release but it's acquired a cult  following over the years there's plenty  of fans hoping that they'll live to see  a kremlin's three  it's one thing not to be interested in a  sequel it's another to be forced into  one thanks to a contract that's exactly  what happened to jan dibont director of  the runaway bus action film speed de  bont felt that the story of speed had  reached its natural conclusion but the  surprise success of the first film meant  he was contractually obligated to make  one anyway thus speed 2 cruise control  was born replacing the bus with a boat  and keanu reeves with jason patrick  speed 2 failed to recapture the  excitement of the original despite  featuring the always entertaining willem  dafoe as the main villain even though it  featured one of the biggest most  expensive movie stunts of the 90s cruise  control is only talked about nowadays  when listing the worst sequels in  cinematic history  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

